<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qudshanis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kochanis, Konak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qudshanis is a village in Hakkâri Province in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. From the 17th century until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> it was the seat of the Shimun line of patriarchs of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-east">Church of the East</a>, who led the Assyrian Christian tribes of the Hakkari mountains. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> were driven from the region during the massacres and wars of 1914–1918, and the patriarchate moved into exile.</p></div>
